MixedCaseValidator
==================

When validating a string attribute, ensure it is not all in capital or
lowercase letters. Values with fewer than three letters that have a case are
skipped, so initials, digits, and scripts without case (e.g. Chinese) never
fail.

Installation
============

Add the gem to your Gemfile:

  gem "validation_kit"

Example
=======

class Person < ActiveRecord::Base
  validates :first_name, mixed_case: true
end

Person.new(first_name: "BOB").valid?  # false: "First name cannot be in all caps"
Person.new(first_name: "bob").valid?  # false: "First name cannot be in all lowercase"
Person.new(first_name: "Bob").valid?  # true

Attribute Names
===============

The %{item} in the message is the attribute's translated name:

en:
  activerecord:
    attributes:
      person:
        first_name: "Given name"

Alternatively, pass the :attribute_name option:

  validates :first_name, mixed_case: { attribute_name: "Given name" }

Without either, the humanized attribute name ("First name") is used.

Error Messages
==============

Errors are added as :all_caps and :all_lowercase, so you can check them with
errors.added?(:first_name, :all_caps) and translate them per model:

en:
  activerecord:
    errors:
      models:
        person:
          attributes:
            first_name:
              all_caps: "Your first name cannot be in all caps"
              all_lowercase: "Your first name cannot be in all lowercase"

or pass the :all_caps and :all_lowercase options:

  validates :first_name, mixed_case: { all_caps: "don't shout at me, bro" }

The default English and French messages live under errors.messages.


